  <ym-title|Native selection and same-family consumer
  binding><label|native-selection-and-same-family-consumer-binding>

  Draft, issue #26; session hairer-codex-existence-20261111. Source pin
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Prose:
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/public-run-binding.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:public-run-binding>. This is a bounded composition argument,
  not a global dependency certificate. Reuse
  <verbatim|public-binding-package-audit.md>; no alternate Roll witness is
  used.

  <section|Exact source route><label|exact-source-route>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>: default dynamics and
    minted custody, garment10, positive b, simple G, trivial eventually-paid
    predicate; invokes the selector below with
    NativeComponentRecipe.Choice/available/floor/numeric and
    ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.postnumeric. Returns
    R,T,W,penalty,Funded,Attached.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>
    and its <verbatim|_of_prediction> version,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodRun.lean>:
    retains penalty, PostnumericPreselection, order/power inequalities,
    selected predicate, TreasuryFunded, CommonPeriodPurchase.Funded, Pillars,
    Funded and further receipts, all on the same R. The public wrapper
    discards standalone order/power, predicate, treasury and period fields.
    Prose retains them at this underlying selector call, not by projecting
    them from Funded.

    <item>Same namespace <verbatim|allFactorWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>
    and <verbatim|_of_prediction>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock.lean>:
    <verbatim|Orders := \<langle\>4,fun i=\<gtr\>6+i,fun i=\<gtr\>2+i,fun
    _=\<gtr\>100\<rangle\>>; fixed parameter support exponent=100 and
    separate budget exponent\<geqslant\>100. The original Sheet/quote are
    chosen before demand, blockFloor and lengths; actual lengths precede
    postnumeric cost. Native orders are lower bounds, not exact derivative
    order=6+i after profile enlargement. h100 uses params_eq and
    HStage.prices.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Integration.ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.{on_run,Attached,of_preselection}>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.lean>:
    kernel, stage, lengths and sufficient horizon are obtained from the
    actual R.alloy.B.valid and R.alloy.B.plan. The floor inequality uses
    R.rolls.large. Realized is on R.family.path.levels and R.alloy.B.M, not
    another realization.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Integration.NativeComponentRecipe.{Choice,available,floor,width,numeric,post,openBook_of_stagePaid,Realized,realize}>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativeComponentRecipe.lean>: Choice comes
    from RG08.Flat.entrance_gate, Cast.assured, Aura.dual_support; floor is
    the maximum of flat/sworn/dual/Yamen.need/Redo.rail. Numeric is inverse
    width. Post is max(Redo.after,Yamen.shade) at actual lengths. Realize
    projects floors/costs, obtains OpenBook via log(exp) on the identical
    patch, flat Delay via Yamen.hatch/stamped, and applies the three original
    suppliers.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Integration.NativeDiagonalClockRequest.PaidRequests>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativeDiagonalClockRequest.lean>, and
    <verbatim|YM.Integration.NativePostLengthPayment.StagePaid>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePostLengthPayment.lean>: the former
    has \<forall\>E\<exists\>first\<forall\>m\<geqslant\>first\<forall\>j\<leqslant\>J(m+1)
    with \|F E j\|\<leqslant\>1+loglog(hatBeta m); the latter is
    \<forall\>m,F(J(m+1))\<leqslant\>hatBeta m. They must not be interchanged
    at stage zero.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Consumer map and retained hypotheses><label|consumer-map-and-retained-hypotheses>

  In <verbatim|Lean/YM/R2I/Campaign/Accepted.lean>, namespace
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.Funded>:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|gallery> and <verbatim|coverage> evaluate
    <verbatim|attentive> on literal <verbatim|R.T R.tuning.receipts R.t
    R.accepts R.stories R.doors R.makes R.carries R.books>. Canonical proof:
    original-history-portfolio-attachment.tex; no duplicate derivation of
    service estimates here.

    <item><verbatim|jewel> uses W, simple G and the retained same-run sky,
    locrian and wild inputs.

    <item><verbatim|logPackage> uses W, poly, halo, same sky, silk, tic,
    fixed=100 and logCopy. The last clock tends to infinity by composing
    logCopy with the actual deep J. Canonical
    common-funded/common-observable/common-scale and ope-scale/ope-history
    chapters remain responsible for their estimates.

    <item><verbatim|YM.R2IGoals.fromFunded> first takes the coupling
    extraction via PertExtension.Running.extraction, then R.extractible17 on
    that refinement. The selected Final, phase transport, reader and all
    endpoint properties share its table. The combined refinement is g.refine
    w. Coupling limits use Extraction.Order.retained; full mesh uses
    hJ.fullMesh through from_spec, not a conclusion from subsequence
    extraction alone. Trace uses H.gallery; mantle uses H.coverage. Separate
    OPE prescription quantifiers remain as in the endpoint; the prose does
    not identify all prescriptions.
  </itemize-minus>

  The prose assumes the analytic interfaces of the canonical chapters and
  only establishes identity and simultaneous retention. No new proof of
  Pupil, actual reader comparisons, trace sensor/branch tasks, or a global
  closure claim is made. NativeComponentRecipe explicitly does not itself
  supply the full joint qlocal selection. Formal record names and discarded
  wrapper fields remain in this blueprint rather than the mathematical text.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  Read exact declarations and definitions above using scoped rg/sed/cat; read
  the existing five canonical chapters/audit and original-history attachment.
  Literature treatment: elementary simultaneous witness retention,
  monotonicity and preservation of limits; no external theorem replaces an
  analytic supplier. No Lean edits or fresh Lean build/axiom replay.
  Independent review and LaTeX integration pending.

